# Inject Dispatchers

Never use `Dispatchers.Default`, `Dispatchers.IO`, `Dispatchers.Main`, or
`Dispatchers.Main.immediate` directly in production (`*Main`) code.

Bind them once in `dispatchersModule` (`:core:common`) and inject `CoroutineDispatcher` at call
sites:

| Qualifier | Binds |
| --- | --- |
| `DefaultDispatcher` | `Dispatchers.Default` |
| `IoDispatcher` | `Dispatchers.IO` |
| `MainDispatcher` | `Dispatchers.Main` |
| `MainImmediateDispatcher` | `Dispatchers.Main.immediate` |

```kotlin
// ❌ BAD
CoroutineScope(SupervisorJob() + Dispatchers.Default)
.withContext(Dispatchers.Main) { … }

// ✅ GOOD
CoroutineScope(SupervisorJob() + get<CoroutineDispatcher>(DefaultDispatcher))
.withContext(get<CoroutineDispatcher>(MainDispatcher)) { … }
```

Do not bind or inject `Dispatchers.Unconfined` for production — use it only in tests when
intentional.

Exceptions: test code (`*Test`), and the single binding site inside `dispatchersModule`.
